			<TABLE class="content_text" WIDTH="95%" BORDER="0" CELLSPACING="0" CELLPADDING="0">
				<TR>
					<TD>
						<P CLASS="content_heading1">
							Laplink Internet Security Support
							<hr noshade size="1">
						<p class="content_heading2">Frequently Asked Questions</p>
						<UL>
							<LI>
								<A HREF="#a">When I access my PC using Laplink Internet, what stops a third 
									party from seeing my information as it travels over the Internet?</A>
							<LI>
								<A HREF="#b">What keeps a third party from hacking your servers to access my 
									information?</A>
							<LI>
								<A HREF="#c">What keeps a third party from bypassing your secure servers and 
									accessing my PC directly?</A>
						</UL>
						<hr noshade size="1">
					</TD>
				</TR>
				<TR>
					<TD>
						<a name="a"></a><B>When I access my PC sing Laplink Internet, what stops a 
							third party from seeing my information as it travels over the Internet?</B>
						<BR>
						The Laplink Internet service supports 128 bit end-to-end encryption. We 
						leverage HTTPS to securely transmit your information over the Internet, using 
						Secure Socket Layer (SSL) encryption.<br>
						<br>
						This is the same technology used by major e-commerce sites to securely transmit 
						credit card information over the Internet. You can verify that you have 
						end-to-end encryption by confirming that your browser is showing a small yellow 
						padlock in the lower right area.
						<P></P>
						<P CLASS="BOTTOMNAV"><A HREF="#top"><IMG SRC="x-res/TOP.GIF" BORDER="0"></A>
							<hr noshade size="1">
					</TD>
				</TR>
				<TR>
					<TD>
						<a name="b"></a><B>What keeps a third party from hacking your servers to access my 
							information?</B>
						<BR>
						We NEVER store any of your data on our 
						servers; instead, our servers simply request and format the information 
						directly from your PC each time you request 
						something.
						<P></P>
						<p>We do store your Laplink Internet password on our servers and have implemented 
							multiple levels of security to protect your password...</p>
						<p>
							1) Passwords are stored using non-reversible MD5 encryption (even our internal 
							staff cannot access passwords)<br>
							<br>
							2) Our servers are located in a high security data center with restricted 
							physical access based on biometric hand scanners<br>
							<br>
							3) High security servers with restricted internal access based on security 
							policy
							<br>
							<br>
							4) Failed logins have a long delay which makes it difficult for someone to try 
							lots of passwords quickly</p>
						<P CLASS="BOTTOMNAV"><A HREF="#top"><IMG SRC="x-res/TOP.GIF" BORDER="0"></A>
							<hr noshade size="1">
					</TD>
				</TR>
				<TR>
					<TD>
						<a name="c"></a><B>What keeps a third party from bypassing your secure servers and 
							accessing my PC directly?</B>
						<BR>
						Laplink Internet never accepts socket requests; instead, Laplink Internet 
						creates a connection with our servers and only receives information requests 
						from our servers via this connection.
						<P CLASS="BOTTOMNAV"><A HREF="#top"><IMG SRC="x-res/TOP.GIF" BORDER="0"></A>
							<hr noshade size="1">
					</TD>
				</TR>
			</TABLE>
			<!-- End Content Area -->
